  <text>
    <body>
      <div type="clause" n="17.1">
        <head><ref type="lawCode" target="law:IICn">II Cn</ref> 17.1</head>
        <ab type="liebermannText" xml:lang="ang" source="#liebermann" n="17.1" corresp="#wit-g-a"><pb n="320" ed="#liebermann"/>And sece man hundredes gemot<ptr type="liebermannNote" n="17" target="#IICn_17-1.lnote.oe.17"/> be wíte, eallswa hit<ptr type="liebermannNote" n="**" target="#IICn_17-1.lnote.oe.star2"/> is to secenne.<ptr type="liebermannNote" n="18" target="#IICn_17-1.lnote.oe.18"/></ab>
        <ab type="liebermannText" xml:lang="ang" source="#liebermann" n="17.1" corresp="#wit-b"><pb n="320" ed="#liebermann"/>Sece man his hundred. Séce man hundredes gemót be wíte, ealswa hit riht is to secanne.</ab>
        <ab type="liebermannText" xml:lang="ang" source="#liebermann" n="17.1" corresp="#wit-a"><pb n="320" ed="#liebermann"/>And sece man hundredes gemot be wite, ealswa hit rih[t]<ptr type="liebermannNote" n="4" target="#IICn_17-1.lnote.oe.4"/> is to seacan.</ab>
        <ab type="liebermannText" xml:lang="la" source="#liebermann" n="17.1" corresp="#wit-q"><pb n="321" ed="#liebermann"/>Et requiratur hundretum super witam, sicut iustum est.</ab>
        <ab type="liebermannText" xml:lang="la" source="#liebermann" n="17.1" corresp="#wit-cons-cn"><pb n="321" ed="#liebermann"/>Centenariique conuentus adeatur super forefacturam, secundum quod rectum est aditu.</ab>
        <ab type="editionText" xml:lang="ang" source="#robertson" n="17.1" corresp="#wit-b"><pb n="182" ed="#robertson"/>Sece man his hundred. Séce man hundredes gemót be wíte, ealswa hit riht<ptr type="editorNote" n="1" target="#IICn_17-1.robnote.fn.1"/> is to secanne.</ab>
        <ab type="editionText" xml:lang="ang" source="#rabin-doml" corresp="#wit-g-a"><pb n="262" ed="#rabin-doml"/>And sece man hundredes gemot be wite, eallswa hit is to secenne.</ab>
        <ab type="translation" xml:lang="de" source="#liebermann"><pb n="321" ed="#liebermann"/>(Besuche man sein Hundert. <hi rend="italic">B</hi>) Und man besuche das Hundertschaftsgericht bei Strafe<ptr type="liebermannNote" n="1" target="#IICn_17-1.lnote.de.1"/>, so wie es richtig<ptr type="liebermannNote" n="2" target="#IICn_17-1.lnote.de.2"/> (<hi rend="italic">fehlt G</hi>) ist zu besuchen.</ab>
        <ab type="translation" xml:lang="en" source="#claude" ana="#fromGerman">(Let one attend one's hundred. B) And let the hundred-court be attended on pain of a fine, as it is right (lacking in G) to attend it.</ab>
        <ab type="translation" xml:lang="en" source="#robertson" corresp="#wit-b"><ptr type="editorNote" n="1" target="#IICn_17-1.robnote.n.1"/><pb n="183" ed="#robertson"/>Everyone shall attend his hundred [court]. Everyone shall attend the hundred court, under pain of fine<ptr type="editorNote" n="2" target="#IICn_17-1.robnote.n.2"/>, whenever he is required by law to attend it.</ab>
        <ab type="translation" xml:lang="en" source="#rabin-doml" corresp="#wit-g-a"><pb n="263" ed="#rabin-doml"/>And everyone is to attend the hundred court whenever summoned or suffer a penalty.</ab>
        <note type="comparison" source="#liebermann" n="321"><ref target="clause:IIIEg_5">III Eg 5</ref></note>
        <note type="comparisonPrinted" source="#liebermann">ebd. 5</note>
        <note type="comparison" source="#wormald-mel" n="358"><label>source (roman)</label> <ref target="clause:IIIEg_5">III Eg 5–5.1</ref> <quote>Table 5.4, II Cn 17:1-18: III Eg 5-5:1</quote></note>
        <note type="editorial">‘riht’ is supplied in G from the other MSS. B's heading is red. Liebermann compares III Eg 5.; BR: added from Gesetze I p. 321, October 2026 (MS Cons)</note>
        <note type="textual" source="#rabin-doml">And . . . hundredes: Sece man his hundred B</note>
        <note type="textual" source="#rabin-doml">hit is: hit riht is AB</note>
        <note type="liebermannNote" subtype="textual" xml:id="IICn_17-1.lnote.oe.17" n="17" source="#liebermann"><bibl><biblScope unit="volume">1</biblScope><biblScope unit="page">320</biblScope></bibl><seg type="original" xml:lang="de">-te <hi rend="italic">Ld</hi></seg><seg type="translation" xml:lang="en" source="#claude">-te Ld</seg></note>
        <note type="liebermannNote" subtype="textual" xml:id="IICn_17-1.lnote.oe.star2" n="**" source="#liebermann"><bibl><biblScope unit="volume">1</biblScope><biblScope unit="page">320</biblScope></bibl><seg type="original" xml:lang="de"><hi rend="italic">ergänze</hi> riht <hi rend="italic">aus übrigen</hi></seg><seg type="translation" xml:lang="en" source="#claude">supply riht from the others</seg></note>
        <note type="liebermannNote" subtype="textual" xml:id="IICn_17-1.lnote.oe.18" n="18" source="#liebermann"><bibl><biblScope unit="volume">1</biblScope><biblScope unit="page">320</biblScope></bibl><seg type="original" xml:lang="de">seacan <hi rend="italic">Ld</hi></seg><seg type="translation" xml:lang="en" source="#claude">seacan Ld</seg></note>
        <note type="liebermannNote" subtype="textual" xml:id="IICn_17-1.lnote.oe.4" n="4" source="#liebermann"><bibl><biblScope unit="volume">1</biblScope><biblScope unit="page">320</biblScope></bibl><seg type="original" xml:lang="de">rih <hi rend="italic">A</hi></seg><seg type="translation" xml:lang="en" source="#claude">rih A</seg></note>
        <note type="liebermannNote" subtype="erklaerung" xml:id="IICn_17-1.lnote.de.1" n="1" source="#liebermann-erkl"><bibl><biblScope unit="volume">3</biblScope><biblScope unit="page">205</biblScope><biblScope unit="column">1</biblScope></bibl><seg type="original" xml:lang="de">Schwerlich Wergeld, das <hi rend="italic">u</hi>. 83 fordert, für Trotz gegen dieses Gesetz allgemein, sondern nur ein Strafgeldfixum (<hi rend="italic">s. d. Gl</hi> 5), vermutlich 30 Schill.</seg><seg type="translation" xml:lang="en" source="#claude">Hardly wergild, which <hi rend="italic">below</hi> 83 demands for defiance of this law in general, but only a fixed fine (<hi rend="italic">see</hi> that word in <hi rend="italic">Gl</hi> 5), presumably 30 shill.</seg></note>
        <note type="liebermannNote" subtype="erklaerung" xml:id="IICn_17-1.lnote.de.2" n="2" source="#liebermann-erkl"><bibl><biblScope unit="volume">3</biblScope><biblScope unit="page">205</biblScope><biblScope unit="column">1</biblScope></bibl><seg type="original" xml:lang="de">Die Zufügung <hi rend="italic">ante hoc factum est</hi> in Inst scheint Reminiszenz an III Eg 5 <hi rend="italic">hit ær geset wæs</hi></seg><seg type="translation" xml:lang="en" source="#claude">The addition <hi rend="italic">ante hoc factum est</hi> in Inst seems to be a reminiscence of III Eg 5 <hi rend="italic">hit ær geset wæs</hi></seg></note>
        <note type="editorNote" subtype="endnote" xml:id="IICn_17-1.robnote.n.1" n="1" source="#robertson"><bibl><biblScope unit="page">354</biblScope></bibl><seg type="original" xml:lang="en">Cf. III Edg. 5.</seg></note>
        <note type="editorNote" subtype="endnote" xml:id="IICn_17-1.robnote.n.2" n="2" source="#robertson"><bibl><biblScope unit="page">354</biblScope></bibl><seg type="original" xml:lang="en">Does this mean 30 shillings?</seg></note>
        <note type="editorNote" subtype="footnote" xml:id="IICn_17-1.robnote.fn.1" n="1" source="#robertson"><bibl><biblScope unit="page">182</biblScope></bibl><label>híne</label><seg type="original" xml:lang="en">Om. G.</seg></note>
      </div>
    </body>
